            "sv_kind": "ProceduralBlockSymbol:initialized-variable",
            "text": "always_ff writes 'y', which has a declaration initializer: IEEE 1800-2023 counts the initialization as a procedural assignment (\u00a76.5, \u00a710.5) and forbids any other process to assign an always_ff variable (\u00a79.2.2.2, \u00a79.2.2.4); Xcelium 24.03 rejects the design (*E,MULAXX) where Icarus 12.0, Yosys 0.53 and slang run it, so the tools split on its legality (drop the initializer, or write the variable from a plain `always` procedure)"
